  "closed_avenues": [
    "hardware W4A16 cannot consume the original E2M1 codes: the released code-to-value map is not two's-complement int4, so the INT8 widening is inherent to the format",
    "wider element access buys about 10% (0.2493 ms against 0.2770 ms at two bytes per lane, byte identical) and the four-byte form aborts the Ascend Triton compiler; the released kernel matches a decode-free copy at 64-84 GB/s, so that is the Triton path's cap"
  ],
